---
description: Centralaizer shared-memory hub — recall before, remember after
alwaysApply: true
---

This machine runs **Centralaizer**, a local shared-memory hub (MCP server `centralaizer`,
http://localhost:3000, zero cloud egress) holding context from every AI tool the user works with —
so knowledge from one tool/session is available in the next.

- **Before** starting any non-trivial task, call the `memory_search` tool with the user's request
  (or its key terms) to pull relevant prior decisions, fixes, and facts. Use anything relevant and
  say when you did.
- **After** you make a durable decision, discover a fact, or land a fix, call `memory_write` with a
  concise 1–2 sentence summary so the next session — in any tool — has it.
- Skip both only for trivial edits. Never invent memories — persist only what actually happened.
